{:adr/id "2607122200"
 :adr/title "wire physics-2d into kami-engine's ECS via kotoba.physics.contract"
 :adr/status :accepted
 :adr/date "2026-07-12"
 :adr/related ["2607121900-raycast-host-binding"
               "2607102200-west-manifest-api-single-entry"]

 :gap "kotoba.physics.contract (kotoba-lang/physics) already had 3 backends -- physics-2d.backend (:realtime, rigid-body-2d), cae.backend (:high-fidelity, CFD/FEM/process/materials/emag/production-des), kami-engine-vphysics (vehicle, out of scope) -- but NONE had any consumer anywhere in the monorepo. kami-engine itself has zero live Rust ECS (staleness-notice-verified); the real browser host is kotoba-lang/host's kami.host, whose kami:engine/physics@1.0.0 import (apply-impulse) was always a no-op stub. network-isekai already had a SEPARATE isekai.physics bridge wired through the same contract, but it only powers a window.__physics verification probe with its own disjoint entity set -- never hooked into the game's actual ECS, so no game's renderer/guest ever saw its results. Read cae.industrial.cljc in full (423 lines) looking for a genuine closed-form cross-check for physics-2d's actual domain (2D rigid-body collision/impulse dynamics) -- found NONE: cfd/fem/process/materials/emag/production-des are all static/steady-state/queueing models, no free-body/projectile/rigid-body-collision case anywhere. Forcing a mapping would be fabricated."

 :decision "Add a rigid-body-2d ECS system to kami.host (kotoba-lang/host): attach-rigid-body!/detach-rigid-body!/set-rigid-body-gravity!/rigid-body-ids/step-rigid-bodies!. step-rigid-bodies! (called once per tick! frame) projects tagged entities into kotoba.physics.contract/make-scene, steps them via physics-2d.backend/backend, writes results back onto the ECS -- through the shared contract, not a bespoke ad-hoc loop, mirroring the existing :platformer convention's shape but delegating physics to physics-2d. tick!'s ad-hoc gravity/plain-integration and resolve-collisions!'s layer push-apart both exclude rigid-body-2d ids so the two systems never double-drive an entity. network-isekai forwards a new :rigid-body-2d scene key (same pattern as :platformer), with a doc comment disambiguating it from the pre-existing isekai.physics verification-only bridge. kami-engine's CLAUDE.md gets a pointer to this wiring plus a cross-reference to kami-engine's own concurrently-merged kami-physics/ (PR #100, kami.physics.runtime -- a backend-id router with no ECS of its own; kami.host talks to physics-2d.backend directly instead, to avoid pulling vehicle/CAE backends into a browser bundle that never needs them). Verification tests in physics-2d ground the realtime approximation in analytic mechanics (Newton's law of impact, momentum conservation, elastic-collision KE conservation, exact symplectic-Euler closed form under gravity, free-fall+bounce chained end-to-end) instead of cae.industrial, per the honest no-overlap finding -- all exercised through contract/step + physics-2d.backend/backend, the real production path."

 :verification {:physics-2d "clojure -M:test: 9 tests / 24 assertions, 0 failures; clojure -M:lint: 0 errors. New test/physics_2d/analytic_mechanics_verification_test.cljc"
                :host "clojure -M:test: 8 tests / 16 assertions, 0 failures; clojure -M:lint: 0 errors. New test/kami/host_rigid_body_test.clj (JVM-runnable, no WebAssembly instance needed -- attach/detach, free-fall integration, momentum-conserving collision through the ECS write-back path)"
                :network-isekai "single-line change in isekai.game.cljc, pattern-mirrored against the already-working :platformer forwarding line; clj-kondo syntax pass clean (repo has no standalone :test/:lint alias to run in-project; the two exists?/array-seq errors from an isolated single-file lint are cljs-core false positives of linting outside the project's shadow-cljs config)"
                :kami-engine "doc-only change (CLAUDE.md); no test surface"}

 :consequences ["a game/scene authored against kotoba-lang/host can now attach real rigid-body physics to any entity and get correct impulse-resolved collisions/gravity/positional-correction each frame without hand-writing a physics loop"
                "physics-2d.backend now has two real consumers: kami.host's rigid-body-2d ECS system (gameplay-affecting, this ADR) and isekai.physics (pre-existing, verification-probe only, unaffected/untouched)"
                "kami-engine-cae-solver remains entirely unconsumed by this integration path -- honest finding: its domain (static structural/CFD/process/materials/emag/DES screening) has no genuine overlap with realtime rigid-body dynamics; no code there was changed"
                "kami-engine-vphysics untouched (vehicle-specific, out of scope)"
                "known gap: the WASM guest ABI's own kami:engine/physics@1.0.0/apply-impulse import stays a no-op -- a compiled .kotoba/.cljc guest cannot itself author a rigid-body component through the wasm boundary yet, only the host app can (network-isekai's scene EDN or any future kami.host consumer); extending the guest ABI itself would need kotoba.engine-clj's host-import ABI + kototama's codegen updated in lockstep, out of scope here"]

